1
00:00:00,192 --> 00:00:04,014
The last extension I personally like having

2
00:00:04,126 --> 00:00:05,940
is the Subagents extension,

3
00:00:06,518 --> 00:00:09,730
Pi Subagents, also by Nico Priem, the same

4
00:00:09,826 --> 00:00:12,620
person who created that Web Access

5
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:13,086
extension.

6
00:00:13,824 --> 00:00:17,068
And Subagents allows Pi to create and spin

7
00:00:17,116 --> 00:00:20,006
up subagents in its main session so that it

8
00:00:20,006 --> 00:00:23,009
can offload certain work like research work

9
00:00:23,458 --> 00:00:25,866
to subagents which have their own fresh

10
00:00:26,107 --> 00:00:28,593
context window and don't pollute the main

11
00:00:28,689 --> 00:00:29,491
context window

12
00:00:30,116 --> 00:00:32,441
and can then report back to the main agent

13
00:00:32,441 --> 00:00:34,430
once they're done. This is a feature many

14
00:00:34,526 --> 00:00:36,707
coding agents like Claude Code have built

15
00:00:36,771 --> 00:00:39,658
in. Pi does not, but because it's so

16
00:00:39,658 --> 00:00:42,320
extensible, there are packages like this

17
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:44,309
which add this feature. And it is a feature

18
00:00:44,389 --> 00:00:47,901
I personally like having. So it is another

19
00:00:47,917 --> 00:00:50,243
extension I installed. That's the command

20
00:00:50,243 --> 00:00:51,205
for installing it.

21
00:00:52,506 --> 00:00:53,518
Py install npm

22
00:00:54,113 --> 00:00:55,093
py-subagents.

23
00:00:55,719 --> 00:00:56,941
With that, it is available.

24
00:00:57,648 --> 00:00:58,885
And if you then start Pi,

25
00:00:59,640 --> 00:00:59,945
you can

26
00:01:00,524 --> 00:01:03,914
run /subagents doctor to show some

27
00:01:03,914 --> 00:01:04,862
diagnostics.

28
00:01:05,505 --> 00:01:07,304
And this also should show you

29
00:01:07,995 --> 00:01:10,791
how many subagents are available because

30
00:01:11,048 --> 00:01:13,169
just installing this extension already sets

31
00:01:13,298 --> 00:01:16,897
up some subagents. But you can then also, as

32
00:01:17,010 --> 00:01:19,146
always, dive into the official docs of this

33
00:01:19,259 --> 00:01:21,845
package to configure it in greater detail.

34
00:01:22,472 --> 00:01:24,561
Again, not something you have to do, not

35
00:01:24,561 --> 00:01:27,019
something I did. I'm fine with the built-in

36
00:01:27,308 --> 00:01:29,509
subagents you have, which are already

37
00:01:29,926 --> 00:01:32,127
prepared for the most common tasks like

38
00:01:32,127 --> 00:01:34,087
exploring the file system or doing

39
00:01:34,184 --> 00:01:36,770
researching, but you can tweak everything to

40
00:01:36,770 --> 00:01:38,538
your liking if you want to.

41
00:01:39,180 --> 00:01:42,024
You can use the regular Pi settings file for

42
00:01:42,217 --> 00:01:44,675
overriding package-specific settings, for

43
00:01:44,723 --> 00:01:46,829
this subagents package. And you can also use

44
00:01:46,829 --> 00:01:48,951
the local settings file instead if you have

45
00:01:48,983 --> 00:01:51,941
project-specific overrides or changes. If

46
00:01:51,941 --> 00:01:52,166
you run

47
00:01:52,938 --> 00:01:54,417
/subagents/models,

48
00:01:55,012 --> 00:01:58,227
you see which AI models will be used for the

49
00:01:58,227 --> 00:01:59,674
different subagents.

50
00:02:00,221 --> 00:02:02,214
And you can also easily tweak them, as

51
00:02:02,262 --> 00:02:03,243
you'll see in the next lecture.
